    "model": "Osmosis is the net movement of water molecules from a region of higher water concentration to a region of lower water concentration across a semi-permeable membrane. It differs from active transport in that osmosis is passive and needs no ATP, whereas active transport needs energy from ATP made in respiration. Osmosis moves water down a concentration gradient, whereas active transport moves substances against the concentration gradient, from low to high concentration. Osmosis moves only water, whereas active transport moves particular solutes such as ions and glucose.",
