    "model": "The part of the brain that controls breathing is the medulla oblongata, which contains the breathing centre. The concentration of carbon dioxide is detected by central chemoreceptors in the medulla oblongata, close to the breathing centre, and by peripheral chemoreceptors in the carotid bodies, in the walls of the carotid arteries in the neck, and in the aortic bodies, in the wall of the arch of the aorta.",
