    "model": "(i) Increased air movement increases the rate of transpiration. Wind blows away the layer of humid air that builds up around the leaf, so the outside air stays dry and the water vapour concentration gradient between the leaf and the air stays steep, so water vapour diffuses out faster. (ii) Increased light intensity increases the rate of transpiration. Stomata open in the light and close in darkness, so with more light they open wider, giving more diffusion of water vapour out of the leaf, until the stomata are fully open.",
