    "marks": 6,
    "model": "Predation is a feeding relationship in which one animal, the predator, kills and eats another, the prey. Fox (predator): acute hearing and smell to find prey, forward-facing eyes for judging distance, and hunting mostly at night, when rabbits feed. Rabbit (prey): eyes on the sides of the head, giving an almost all-round field of view, so that it can see danger coming.",
    "prompt": "What is meant by predation? Give one adaptation of a named predator and one of its named prey from an ecosystem you studied.",
    "type": "short"
