    "model": "Bioinformatics is the use of computers and software to store, search, compare and analyse biological information, especially DNA, RNA and protein sequences. Two reasons why computers are needed: one human genome is about 3 billion base pairs, and sequencing machines produce data on many genomes quickly, which no person could read or compare by eye; and computers compare sequences in seconds, store them permanently and let scientists anywhere share them.",
    "prompt": "What is meant by bioinformatics? Give two reasons why computers are needed to analyse genetic information.",
